; E170 Phase 12, G2 -- AN EDITED FIXTURE IS REFUSED.
;
; The defect this closes: `oracle-ask`'s `or-fixed` arm opened the named path,
; read it, and returned its bytes WITHOUT EVER CONSULTING `dg`. So rank 2 -- "a
; fixed committed artifact, or a reference outside BOTH legs", the rank that
; caught E161 G0 -- was a path plus an argument nothing looked at, and an anchor
; edited after the fact was honoured in full. `e168_rank_floor.chiral:43-56` wrote
; that gap down in its own comment and named its condition for closure: "a floor
; that OPENS the named path and compares the digest before honouring rank 2".
; This is that floor, and this fixture is what makes it a claim that can fail.
;
; The digest IS the bytes, and no hash is invented -- testing-floors.md:250-252
; sanctions exactly that, and admission clause 5 (small enough to review) is what
; makes it buildable. The two constraints are one design.
;
; The anchor is not minted to justify a sentence, which is the thing
; e168_rank_floor refused. `scaffold/tests/fixed/end-module-prelude.txt` holds the
; exact bytes BOTH module providers emit after the `prelude` module --
; bin/chirality-resolve.sh's emit loop and resolve.chiral's `concat-mods`, which are
; pinned byte-for-byte against each other and were STILL both wrong once: E161 G0
; reported ok with both legs emitting the same wrong marker, and only a fixed
; expectation outside both legs saw it. The negative control is that defect as a
; file: the same line with the closing quote dropped.
;
; Paths are REPO-ROOT-relative and this program is run from the repo root.
;
; exit 0 = every case; otherwise the number of the first failing case:
;   1  a hand-minted anchor is refused by the licence rule (D2 inverted)
;   2  a CCOMP-minted artifact is ADMITTED -- committing one is distribution,
;      which is what keeps the DDC path inside INRIA's non-commercial licence
;   3  the committed anchor is not there
;   4  asking a fixed port tried to BUILD something
;   5  the committed anchor does not match its own digest -- the anchor rotted
;   6  it matched, but the bytes handed back are not the bytes asked for
;   7  the negative control is not there
;   8  asking for the negative control tried to build something
;   9  THE ROW: the EDITED file was ACCEPTED at rank 2 -- this is the case that
;      is green before W0.3 and red after, and dropping the `bytes=?` comparison
;      from `oracle-ask` puts it back
;   10 `or-fixed` stopped ranking 2
;
; ⚑ WHAT THIS FIXTURE DELIBERATELY DOES NOT TEST, and why the omission is the
; honest answer rather than a gap. The first draft had a fourth ask against an
; ABSENT path, to keep `ob-nofile` and `ob-nomatch` visibly apart. `ledger-lint`
; check S -- which lands in the same wave -- convicted it, correctly: naming an
; untracked path in an `or-fixed` is exactly the laundering the check exists to
; refuse, and a negative control does not get an exemption the next launder could
; hide behind. Case 7 already asserts the direction W0.3 changed (an existing
; file whose bytes are wrong is NOT reported as missing); the other direction is
; `openat` returning a negative fd, which `e168_cap_thread` already covers on a
; path that is not an anchor claim at all.

(import "evidence/test-floor")

(def anchor-path   Str "scaffold/tests/fixed/end-module-prelude.txt")
(def tampered-path Str "scaffold/tests/fixed/end-module-prelude-tampered.txt")

; the digest, which is the bytes, sitting inside the gate file exactly as
; admission clause 5 requires.
(def anchor-bytes Bytes (str->bytes "\n(end-module \"prelude\")\n"))

; ⚑ Recorded as `or-native` because that is what an in-tree hand-written file is
; -- an in-tree provider -- and `Minting` records WHERE THE BYTES CAME FROM, not
; how strong an opinion they are. The rank is `or-fixed`'s (2), decided by
; `oid-prov` on the port and not by this record.
(def anchor-mint Minting
  (minted-by (or-native "written by hand from E161's module-marker rule") "2026-08-25"))

; the minting D2 forbids: committing a ccomp-built artifact IS distributing one.
(def forbidden-mint Minting (minted-by (or-ccomp "3.17") "2026-08-25"))

(def no-input Bytes (str->bytes ""))

(def compile-main (=> I64 I64)
  (lam (n)
    (case (mint-licensed? anchor-mint)
      (false 1)
      (true
        (case (mint-licensed? forbidden-mint)
          (true 2)
          (false
            (case (oracle-ask (builder "B1") (oracle (or-fixed anchor-path anchor-bytes)) no-input)
              ((ob-nofile p b)   (case b ((builder v) 3)))
              ((ob-nobuild w b)  (case b ((builder v) 4)))
              ((ob-nomatch p b)  (case b ((builder v) 5)))
              ((ob-ok o b)
                (case (obs-cmp (ob-bytes anchor-bytes) o)
                  ((ck-fail g w) (case b ((builder v) 6)))
                  ((ck-pass)
                    (case (oracle-ask b (oracle (or-fixed tampered-path anchor-bytes)) no-input)
                      ((ob-nofile p2 b2)  (case b2 ((builder v) 7)))
                      ((ob-nobuild w2 b2) (case b2 ((builder v) 8)))
                      ((ob-ok o2 b2)      (case b2 ((builder v) 9)))
                      ((ob-nomatch p2 b2)
                        (case b2
                          ((builder v)
                            (case (=i (prov-rank (oid-prov (or-fixed anchor-path anchor-bytes))) 2)
                              (true  0)
                              (false 10))))))))))))))))
